# Line endings are LF in this repository, on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference. Files here are GENERATED and then compared byte for
# byte against a fresh render — docs/IPC-SECURITY-SURFACE.md by
# tests/ipc/doc-freshness.test.js and by `npm run ipc:check`, which the release
# script blocks on. The generators write "\n". A Windows checkout with git's
# default core.autocrlf=true rewrites that to "\r\n" on the way to disk, so the
# on-disk file no longer equals what the generator produces and the freshness
# gate fails on Windows while passing everywhere else — reporting a document as
# out of date when it is identical.
#
# eol=lf makes the checkout match what the generators write, so the comparison
# means what it says on all three platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never normalised — a byte changed inside any of these corrupts the file.
# The two owner-supplied assets are named explicitly because they are not in
# the repository yet and must not be touched when they arrive.
*.ico  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gz   binary
*.zip  binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.node binary
*.sqlite3 binary
assets/crm.ico          binary
src/renderer/logo.png   binary
